the chicken is crispy and crunchy  the waffle is like a cloud that soaks up  all the pear butter  hey i'm raeshawn wilder the creator of  eyes of a foodie  and today we'll be making my peanut  butter chicken and waffles my friend  takia from tasty is going to show you  how to make my signature dish  pear butter adds a classy and elegant  touch to my chicken and waffles  start by adding diced pears and water to  a saucepan  then we'll add our nutmeg cinnamon  cloves and allspice  what a lot of people don't know is that  i'm a flight attendant by day  i've seen a lot of different places been  to a lot of different restaurants which  allowed me to expand my brand as a food  blogger  what's up guys this is isabel foodie and  today i am doing some burgers  in 2017 one of my co-workers told me  that i should audition for masterchef  so i flew to new york city and there  were hundreds of  people there to audition i knew that i  had some competition before me  and to be honest i didn't even make it  past the first round  i went back home to detroit and went  back to work  in october of 2018 masterchef was having  auditions again  this time it was the final round of  auditions  and of course my same co-worker told me  that i should audition again  i had no intentions on going back after  what happened in new york the first year  i finally gave in i had decided to make  a cheesecake  but my oven went out and the flights to  dallas were completely oversold  however i finally made it when the  judges tasted my cookie butter  cheesecake  everyone went crazy and i'm proud to say  that out of 20 000 people who auditioned  i made it to the top 80 cast of master  chef season 10.  once i got eliminated i returned home  and i decided to work on my cheesecakes  if my cheesecakes could wow the judges  are masterchef  and lammy in the top 80. i knew that the  people of detroit would also love them  my cookie butter cheesecake is the one  that made a name for me  since then i've created over 25  different flavors including  strawberry shortcake lemon drop orange  cream dream  and my favorite white chocolate  blueberry crumble  now you may be wondering why i'm showing  you how to make chicken waffles today  well the short answer is if i give you  my money making cheesecake recipe  i'd be out of business having my own  business  is really awesome but what good would it  be if i couldn't help other people  my goal as a chef is to inspire other  young african-american men  i really want to help break the  stereotypes of how the world looks at us  with all that's going on in the world  today with police brutality  protests and the black lives matter  movement i know it can be easy for  people of color to be discouraged or  even negative  but i want to encourage all of us that  we have so much to offer to this world  and it's important that we don't allow  the hurdles that we face or what we see  on the news or what we hear in the media  discourage us from reaching our goals my  food journey hasn't been easy by far  i've been eliminated twice and even  doubt tried to creep in sometimes  but i never allowed those things to  hinder me from trying  i had to encourage myself daily and i  want to encourage everyone to use that  same energy towards anything that you're  passionate about  whether that's food or fighting for what  you believe in  but in the meantime love yourself and  love others  try to find the joy in the little things  i hope my pear butter chicken and  waffles recipe  can help bring a little joy into your  life the waffles are super soft and  crispy  the pear butter had the right amount of  sweetness the chicken  perfectly fried i'm telling you you  can't go wrong with this dish  oh yes  you
 

